  "_comment": "MICRO-SPAZIO-3D p.4 (E.D. 11 Oct 2026) · the base shapes a person sketches a proxy with in the Space. DATA, not code: a new shape is a new entry here. Dimensions in METRES, Y-up (glTF and three.js), each shape born with its base centred on the 3D cursor. Kept in EMStudio and not in s3Dgraphy: it is a palette of the editor, not a term of the EM language — the graph receives only what a proxy always is (a geometry property, its SemanticShape, a proxy_model glb), and EM Tools sketches with Blender's own primitives. If EM Tools wants the same list, the file moves to s3Dgraphy's JSON_config as it is. `primitive` is what `shapes3d.ts` builds: box (size [x, y, z]), cylinder (radius, height, segments), cone (radius, height, segments), sphere (radius), hemisphere (radius), plane (size [x, z]), wedge (size [x, y, z]: a right-angled ramp rising along −z), prism (radius, height, sides), torus (radius, tube), arch (span, ring, depth: a semicircular arch whose intrados has diameter `span`).",
